## Capitalization

the "m" in "members of Congress" is not capitalized

## Theoritical terms

Interbranch representation is a subset of interbranch work that is on behalf of a constituency.
We use them mostly interchangable, but interbranch representation should be used whenever talking about work on behalf of a constituency.
Interbranch work should be used whenever discussing whether interbranch work is representative or not.

Incentives or stratigic behavior in the political environment, should be shortened to
"incentives" or "stratigic incentives" not "political enviroment" unless specifically talking about the political environment.

"higher-performing" rather than "higher quality" ---
in general, avoid discussing legislator "quality" since this is both normative and ambigous

## Empirical terms

"requests" is what legislators make of agenices

"demands" or ____ are what constituents make of legislators

## Use Periods in Acronyms

U.S. not US

## Two words, not one

policy work, not policywork

## Don't hyphenate prefixes

reelection not re-election

preexisting

## Don't hyphenate compound words

supermajority not super-majority

antigovenment not anti-government

recordkeeping

followup

email not e-mail

undercount

overpaid

nonprofit


